{#
    The toolbox declaration widget (SPEC §4.1, §15), as a macro — shared by
    the task's own declaration, every step's, and a conversation's, because
    they are the same declaration at different scopes and in different
    places. Import with:

        {% import '_toolbox.html.twig' as toolbox_ui %}

    Lives at the template root rather than under `task/` for that reason: it
    is no longer only the task editor's widget. A chat is the third caller,
    and the reason it is one macro and not three is the same either way —
    the field names it posts are the contract the parser reads
    (`App\Admin\ToolboxSelection`), so a second copy of this markup would be
    a second chance to post something the parser does not understand.

    Two pickers, one active: `tags` resolves against the discovered catalog
    (task.tags ∩ tool.tags), `explicit` names tools exactly. The inactive
    picker is hidden by the editor script but stays in the DOM, so a mode
    switch never loses what was typed — and the server honours only the
    selected mode's list (TaskEditorSubmission), so the hidden one cannot leak
    into the saved declaration.

    Alongside each checkbox list is a free-text companion: the catalog is
    discovered, not authoritative, so a human must be able to declare a tool
    or tag it does not carry yet. The detail page's preview is what tells them
    when such a declaration resolves to nothing. It is seeded with the
    declared entries the catalog does not offer as a checkbox — otherwise
    reopening and re-saving a task would silently drop them.

    `prefix` is the field-name scope: '' for the task's own declaration
    (top-level field names, `toolbox_mode` — the parser reads the task's
    scalars flat, so the toolbox has to match), 'steps[l][s]' for a step's.

    The checkbox arrays need their empty-bracket suffix OUTSIDE the prefix's
    closing bracket — `steps[0][0][toolbox_tags][]`, never
    `steps[0][0][toolbox_tags[]]`. The latter is not a PHP array at all: the
    parser keeps `toolbox_tags[` as a literal key, so every checked box is
    silently discarded and only the free-text companion survives the save.

    Each free-text companion is seeded only from the declaration that belongs
    to *its own* mode: a tags declaration seeds "More tags" (with the entries
    the catalog does not carry), an explicit declaration seeds "More tools" —
    and never the other way round. Seeding both from the same stored list is
    how a tags task used to arrive with its tags pasted into the tool-name
    field, ready to be saved as tool names by an accidental mode switch.
#}
{% macro toolbox(prefix, values, tags, tools, errors, group, disabled = false) %}
{% set open = prefix == '' ? '' : prefix ~ '[' %}
{% set close = prefix == '' ? '' : ']' %}
{% set name_mode = open ~ 'toolbox_mode' ~ close %}
{% set name_tags = open ~ 'toolbox_tags' ~ close ~ '[]' %}
{% set name_tags_extra = open ~ 'toolbox_tags_extra' ~ close %}
{% set name_tools = open ~ 'toolbox_tools' ~ close ~ '[]' %}
{% set name_tools_extra = open ~ 'toolbox_tools_extra' ~ close %}
{% set mode = values.toolbox_mode|default('tags') %}
{% set declared = values.toolbox|default([]) %}
{# Each panel is seeded only from a declaration in *its own* mode. #}
{% set tag_selection = mode == 'tags' ? declared : [] %}
{% set tool_selection = mode == 'explicit' ? declared : [] %}
{% set unknown = mode == 'tags' ? declared|filter(v => v not in tags) : [] %}
{% set unknown_tools = mode == 'explicit' ? declared|filter(v => v not in tools|map(t => t.name)) : [] %}
<fieldset class="toolbox">
    <legend>Toolbox</legend>

    <div class="radio-row" role="radiogroup" aria-label="How the toolbox is resolved">
        <label class="radio">
            <input type="radio" name="{{ name_mode }}" value="tags"
                   data-toolbox-mode {{ mode == 'tags' ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
            <span>By tag <span class="muted">— the catalog's tools carrying these tags</span></span>
        </label>
        <label class="radio">
            <input type="radio" name="{{ name_mode }}" value="explicit"
                   data-toolbox-mode {{ mode == 'explicit' ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
            <span>Explicit tools <span class="muted">— exactly these, by name</span></span>
        </label>
    </div>

    <div class="toolbox-panel" data-toolbox-panel="tags" {% if mode != 'tags' %}hidden{% endif %}>
        {% if tags is empty %}
            <p class="muted">No tags in the catalog yet — tag tools on the <a href="{{ path('app_tool_list') }}">tool catalog</a> page, or type tags below.</p>
        {% else %}
            <ul class="check-list">
                {% for tag in tags %}
                    <li>
                        <label class="check">
                            <input type="checkbox" name="{{ name_tags }}" value="{{ tag }}"
                                   {{ tag in tag_selection ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
                            <span><code>{{ tag }}</code></span>
                        </label>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
        <label class="field">
            <span>More tags <span class="muted">(comma-separated; for tags the catalog does not carry yet)</span></span>
            <input type="text" name="{{ name_tags_extra }}" value="{{ unknown|join(', ') }}" autocomplete="off"
                   placeholder="e.g. weather, calendar" {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
        </label>
    </div>

    <div class="toolbox-panel" data-toolbox-panel="explicit" {% if mode != 'explicit' %}hidden{% endif %}>
        {% if tools is empty %}
            <p class="muted">No tools in the catalog yet — register a server and sync on the <a href="{{ path('app_tool_list') }}">tool catalog</a> page, or type tool names below.</p>
        {% else %}
            <ul class="check-list">
                {% for tool in tools %}
                    <li>
                        <label class="check">
                            <input type="checkbox" name="{{ name_tools }}" value="{{ tool.name }}"
                                   {{ tool.name in tool_selection ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
                            <span>
                                <code>{{ tool.server.name }}.{{ tool.name }}</code>
                                {% if tool.hasSideEffect %}<span class="muted"> · side effects</span>{% endif %}
                            </span>
                        </label>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
        <label class="field">
            <span>More tools <span class="muted">(comma-separated tool names)</span></span>
            <input type="text" name="{{ name_tools_extra }}" value="{{ unknown_tools|join(', ') }}" autocomplete="off"
                   placeholder="e.g. get_weather" {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
        </label>
    </div>

    {% if errors[group] is defined %}
        <p class="field-error" role="alert">{{ errors[group] }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</fieldset>
{% endmacro %}
